          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "a large basket, for carrying provisions, fish, or other commodities; in later use mostly restricted to those carried by a beast of burden (usually in pairs, one on each side, slung across the back), of no particular size (OED s.v. pannier n.1; MED s.v. panier(e, n.); here as a packing unit for glass candles, dry goods, furs, cheese, glass, mirrors, haberdashery, and fish"
    }
  ],
